# Cloudflare Pages redirects. https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# The first rule that matches wins, so exact paths sit above the splats.
# Pages applies a matching rule even where a file exists at that path, so
# no rule here may match a file the site still serves. Pages can only
# redirect (301/302/303/307/308): an old URL with no new home is left alone
# and gets the real 404 page. Query strings play no part in matching.
#
# www -> apex is NOT handled here: Pages _redirects only matches paths, not
# hostnames. Set it up as a Cloudflare Redirect Rule on the zone instead:
#   when hostname eq "www.krizdingus.com"
#   -> 301 to concat("https://krizdingus.com", http.request.uri.path), preserve query string
# HTTP -> HTTPS is Cloudflare's "Always Use HTTPS" setting (HSTS is in _headers).

